{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"Pe6bcc5c2"},"owner_reference":"#3060","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"Pe6bcc5c2\",\"feature\":\"runtime-hints-r7\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Make backlog_core/server.py's _build_compact_manifest() _hint and _build_over_budget_view() _usage R7-compliant (agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md), and demonstrate both with new tests, without modifying disclosure_handler.py or any existing test assertion.\",\"context\":\"Backlog item: #3060 \\u2014 \\\"fix: runtime hints steer agents away from paginated navigation\\\".\\n\\nSource artifacts (read these, do not rely on this summary):\\n- artifact_read(item_id=3060, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\") \\u2014 plan/architect-runtime-hints-r7.md. Resolved design. Section 2 contains the evidence-based resolution of the ordinal-compatibility open question: the over-budget narrowed hint names `map=True`, NEVER `navigate=<ordinal>`, because `_sections_index_from_result()`'s `[N]` numbers (dict enumeration) and `OrdinalPathMapper`'s ordinals (document-order `[N]`-line parse) are provably non-equivalent under duplicate section titles.\\n- artifact_read(item_id=3060, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\") \\u2014 plan/feature-context-runtime-hints-r7.md.\\n- backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3060\\\", summary=False, section=\\\"RT-ICA\\\") \\u2014 the 2026-08-21 reconciliation entry is authoritative on the signature change.\\n\\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (verbatim from item #3060, entry 2026-08-20T21:51:24Z \\u2014 the plan satisfies these):\\n1. Given `backlog_view(selector=<item>, summary=True)` on an item whose compact manifest is non-empty, the returned `_hint` string's first recommended call is a section-narrowing call (`section=`/`sections=`) \\u2014 not `summary=False`.\\n2. Given `backlog_view(selector=<item>, section=<a single section that is itself over the token budget>)`, where the response is `_over_budget: true`, the returned `_usage` string does not recommend `section=`/`sections=` narrowing again. It names an actually-resolvable next mechanism instead \\u2014 determined by the architect phase's resolution of the ordinal-compatibility open question (RT-ICA reconciliation, 2026-08-21): either (a) `navigate=<ordinal>` where the ordinal is confirmed valid against `OrdinalPathMapper.resolve()`/`valid_ordinals()` for that response, or (b) `map=True` (which needs no address and sidesteps the ordinal-compatibility question), or (c) `navigate=` named only when the response actually carries a resolvable ordinal. Whichever mechanism is chosen, it must not be one already exhausted by the caller.  [RESOLVED BY ARCHITECT: option (b) \\u2014 `map=True`.]\\n3. For any hint string returned by either branch, every parameter address it names (e.g. an ordinal passed to `navigate=`) resolves to a value actually present in the accompanying response's own fields \\u2014 verified by cross-referencing hint content against response content in the same call, and in the `navigate=` case specifically verified against `OrdinalPathMapper.resolve()`, not assumed from `sections_index`'s `[N]` bracket numbers.\\n4. Existing substring assertions continue to pass or are updated in the same change: `test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_view_summary_true_returns_compact_manifest`, `::test_backlog_view_summary_true_hint_contains_selector`, `::test_build_over_budget_view_usage_mentions_sections_param`, `::test_build_over_budget_view_includes_all_nine_fields`, and `test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py`'s `_PASSTHROUGH_LEGACY_KEYS` key-set assertion.\\n5. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_pagination_section_index.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_section_filter_miss.py` exits 0.\\n6. A new test demonstrates: (a) the compact-manifest `_hint` for a narrow-able item does NOT lead with an unqualified `summary=False` suggestion, and (b) the over-budget `_usage` for a request that already narrowed to one section does NOT repeat `section=`/`sections=` advice and DOES name a mechanism that actually resolves per criterion 3 above.\\n\\nSCOPE BOUNDARIES (from grooming \\u2014 violating any of these fails the plan):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` is the ONLY code-change target.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py`, `disclosure_types.py`, `ordinal_mapper.py`, `content_normalizer.py` are reference-only. Do not modify them.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md`, `classifier.md`, `rtica-assessor.md`, `impact-analyst.md` are EXPLICITLY OUT OF SCOPE. No task touches them.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` states R7 and needs no edit.\\n- The 5 test files named in AC5 must keep passing. Existing assertions in them must NOT be rewritten. Appending NEW test functions to two of them is required and sanctioned (architect section 5.4).\\n- Do NOT write `Fixes #3060` / `Closes #3060` / `Resolves #3060` in any commit. Issue closure belongs exclusively to /dh:complete-implementation's final commit step.\\n\\nEXECUTION SHAPE: fully serial T1 -> T2 -> T3. `parallelize-with` is intentionally empty on every task \\u2014 all three tasks depend on the same two files in sequence (implement, then test, then gate). Empty parallelization here is a deliberate conflict-avoidance decision, not an omission.\\n\\nNO BOOKENDS: this plan carries no `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, so no T0/TN bookend tasks are generated. T3 is the plan's own completion gate.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3060\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Make server.py's _hint and over-budget _usage R7-compliant (merged: both hint builders + call-site predicate)\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-20T22:19:25.191213+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"## CoVe Checks\\n\\nAccuracy risk is MEDIUM: this change depends on call-site local names, an in-place-mutation asymmetry between two objects, and a preservation contract against five existing assertions. Verify before committing.\\n\\nKey claims to verify:\\n- The locals `section` and `sections_filter` are genuinely in scope at the `_build_over_budget_view()` call site.\\n- `full_response[\\\"sections\\\"]`, not `result.sections`, reflects plural `sections=[...]` narrowing.\\n- No existing caller passes a 4th positional argument to `_build_over_budget_view()`.\\n\\nVerification questions (each falsifiable):\\n1. Does `grep -n \\\"sections_filter\\\" plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` show an assignment lexically before the `_build_over_budget_view(` call, inside the same `backlog_view()` body? If not, the predicate will `NameError` at runtime.\\n2. Does `_filter_view_sections()`'s docstring or body show it mutating `full_response` while leaving `result` untouched? If it mutates both, requirement 8's rationale is wrong \\u2014 report the discrepancy rather than silently switching to `result.sections`.\\n3. Does `grep -n \\\"_build_over_budget_view(\\\" plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests -r` return only call sites with 3 positional arguments? A 4-positional caller would break on the keyword-only `*`.\\n4. After the edit, does the un-narrowed `_usage` still contain the literal `sections=`, and does `_hint` still contain the literal `summary=False`? If either is gone, AC4's existing assertions break.\\n5. Does the narrowed `_usage` contain any of `sections=['`, `section='0`, `section='/`? It must not. (It DOES contain the bare token `section=` inside the prose \\\"further section= narrowing is not available\\\" \\u2014 that is intentional and correct; only the call-expression forms are prohibited.)\\n\\nEvidence to collect: the grep outputs from questions 1 and 3, the ruff/ty exit codes, and the pytest result from verification step 5.\\n\\nRevision rule: if any check fails or leaves uncertainty, revise the implementation and state in your handoff what changed and why. Do not adjust an existing test to accommodate the change.\",\"description\":\"\",\"objective\":\"`_build_compact_manifest()`'s `_hint` leads with a section-narrowing call, and `_build_over_budget_view()` emits `map=True` guidance when \\u2014 and only when \\u2014 the caller already narrowed to a single section that is still over budget.\",\"requirements\":\"### Scope area A \\u2014 `_build_compact_manifest()` `_hint` reorder\\n\\n1. Swap the two lines of the `_hint` value so the section-narrowing line comes first. The resulting expression must be exactly:\\n\\n```python\\n\\\"_hint\\\": (\\n    f\\\"Load specific sections: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='<index, title, or /regex/>')\\\\n\\\"\\n    f\\\"Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)\\\"\\n),\\n```\\n\\n2. Change nothing else in `_build_compact_manifest()`. No new key, no removed key, no `navigate=`/`map=` suggestion added here (architect section 3.3 \\u2014 `_build_compact_manifest()`'s own `sections_index` carries the same unverified-ordinal exposure, so adding one would repeat the defect this fix resolves elsewhere).\\n\\n### Scope area B \\u2014 `_build_over_budget_view()` signature\\n\\n3. Add a keyword-only parameter with a `False` default, leaving the three existing positional parameters unchanged:\\n\